one and /product/qa-minimal-product rendered the not-found state. localStorage and sessionStorage are both empty and there is no backend API (/api/products returns the Vite index.html), so all product state is in-memory only and resets on every reload or new session.\", \"evidence\": \"admin.products rows: 10 before reload → 9 after reload; Object.keys(localStorage)=[] and Object.keys(sessionStorage)=[].\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 products show exactly one category badge: Tech (Samsung, MacBook, Sony), Home (Breville, Philips Hue, Dyson), Fitness (Bowflex, Theragun, Peloton). Category filter counts 3/3/3 = 9 total. \\\"Featured\\\" is a separate badge, not a category. Admin form offers only these 3 categories.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tags laptop+coffee selected → 2 results (MacBook Pro 14 has laptop, Breville has coffee), i.e. each result has ≥1 selected tag (OR). Adding category=Tech Gadgets narrowed to 1 (MacBook only), so category AND tag-set are both enforced. Earlier: rating≥4.5 + price≤$2,410 returned only products satisfying both.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Publish validation only enforces name and short description; incomplete products can be published\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the Add Product form with ONLY \\\"QA Minimal Product\\\" (name) and a short description succeeded — the product was created and appeared in the admin list (count 9→10). Full review, image URL, affiliate/retailer link and specifications were all left empty and no specification row was added, yet no validation error was shown and publishing was allowed. Price stayed at default 0 and rating 4.5. Only the fully-empty form was rejected, and even then no validation message was displayed.\", \"evidence\": \"Form marks only \\\"Product Name *\\\" and \\\"Short Description *\\\" as required; admin.form.review, admin.form.image-url, admin.form.affiliate-link left blank and zero spec rows still produced a saved product.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/does-not-exist-123 → \\\"Product Not Found — The product you're looking for doesn't exist or has been removed.\\\" with a Browse All Products link and no product.name/product.buy elements. /category/bogus-category → \\\"Category Not Found — The category you're looking for doesn't exist.\\\" with zero product cards rendered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing in search, switching category, changing sort, and adjusting rating/price filters all updated the grid contents, ordering and the \\\"N products found\\\" counter immediately on the same URL (/products) with no manual reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking the product name link for macbook-pro-14 in the grid navigated to /product/macbook-pro-14 showing that same product's data.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking Buy Now on /product/macbook-pro-14 opened a new browser tab at https://example.com/macbook-pro (external host, product-specific path, target=_blank rel=noopener noreferrer). Grid cards use the same per-product external anchors.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Switching category in the filter updates both the trigger's active value (shows \\\"Home Goods\\\"/\\\"Fitness\\\") and the displayed product set/count simultaneously.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/macbook-pro-14 shows name \\\"Apple MacBook Pro 14\\\\\\\"\\\", category badge Tech, rating 4.9, price $1,999, brief description, full 443-char review, 4 tags (laptop/apple/professional/portable), 5 specs (Chip, Memory, Storage, Display, Battery), image alt=\\\"Apple MacBook Pro 14\\\\\\\"\\\", and a Buy Now anchor to https://example.com/macbook-pro.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Seeded tags are category-appropriate: Dyson V15 (Home Goods) → vacuum, cordless, smart-home, cleaning; MacBook Pro (Tech) → laptop, apple, professional, portable. Tag filter \\\"laptop\\\" returned MacBook and \\\"coffee\\\" returned Breville, matching the tags shown on their detail pages; category badges identical between grid and detail.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dyson V15: home featured/latest $749, list \\\"Home | $749 | 4.7 | Intelligent cordless vacuum…\\\", detail identical (Home, $749, 4.7, same description) plus full 424-char review and 5 specs. MacBook: home latest $1,999, category/tech page $1,999, list \\\"Tech | $1,999 | 4.9\\\", detail identical plus full 443-char review ending \\\"…most versatile MacBook ever.\\\" with no truncation (overflow visible).\"}]}"
