    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been tested and recorded: **18 PASS, 4 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary of failures\n\n**FT-2 — Featured products can't be fully browsed.** Marking/unmarking works (unfeaturing Sony correctly swapped in the newly featured kettle), but the homepage caps the featured row at 3 items, and the \"View all\" link `/products?featured=true` ignores the query parameter, rendering all 10 products. There is no featured filter control anywhere, so the complete featured set is unreachable.\n\n**FT-4 — Tag-filter list is hardcoded.** The 35 filter tags are static seed values. New tags saved on products (`qaedittag`, `deep-tissue`, `kettle`, `ceramic`, `qanewtag`) never become filter choices, while tags removed from products (`massage`, `therapy`) remain listed and return \"0 products found\". Notably, keyword search *does* pick up new tags correctly — only the filter list is stale, pointing to a single derivation bug.\n\n**CS-20 — Publish validation is far too permissive.** Only name and short description are enforced. A product saved with no review, no image, no retailer link, and zero specifications published successfully with no validation message — exactly the incomplete record the constraint forbids.\n\n**FT-19 — No persistence.** All state is in-memory: `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` are empty and there is no backend (`/api/products` returns the Vite index HTML). Every create and edit is lost on reload, reverting to the 9 seeded products.\n\n## Notes on what passed\nBrowsing, search, sorting, category filtering, combined-criteria filtering, detail pages, external retailer links, and not-found states all behaved correctly. Admin create/edit itself works well across all three categories and reflects changes immediately, including a correctly re-derived slug when a product is renamed.\n\nTwo incidental observations worth flagging, outside the checklist's scope: the price range slider renders only a \"Minimum\" thumb in the DOM (`role=\"slider\"` count is 1) even though the max value is adjustable and filters correctly — the max thumb is not keyboard-accessible; and the folded `products.grid` collection omits the per-item `buy` control from its `fields` list, so the hints under-report each card's purchase action."
  }
